    "created_at": "2021-12-14T22:40:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-14T22:49:48Z",
    "body": "The best workaround I've found so far is to use `direnv` to change the `STARSHIP_CONFIG` env var to point to a local config.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# project directory\r\n# gcloud related project\r\n\r\n~/project/packages/server\r\n├── .envrc\r\n├── .starship.toml\r\n├── dist\r\n├── package.json\r\n├── src\r\n└── tsconfig.json\r\n```\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# .envrc\r\n\r\nexport STARSHIP_CONFIG=.starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# local config\r\n# .starship.toml\r\n\r\nadd_newline = true\r\n\r\n[gcloud]\r\nformat = 'on [$symbol$project]($style) '\r\n```\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# global config\r\n# ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n\r\nadd_newline = true\r\n\r\n[gcloud]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample\r\n```zsh\r\npackages on GIT main [✘!?]\r\n❯ cd server\r\ndirenv: loading ~/project/packages/server/.envrc\r\ndirenv: export +STARSHIP_CONFIG\r\n\r\nserver on GIT main [✘!?] via NODE v16.13.1 on GCP my-gcp-project\r\n❯ cd ..\r\ndirenv: unloading\r\n\r\npackages on GIT main [✘!?]\r\n❯\r\n```\r\n\r\nObviously its not IDEAL since you have to configure the entire config for each directory, but works for now\r\n\r\n@shinzui",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
