    "created_at": "2023-04-05T10:39:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-05T10:39:45Z",
    "body": "> I think it should be safe to cd into untrusted directories.\r\n\r\nAbsolutely, which is why direnv explicitly requires you `direnv allow` when it detects a new or modified .envrc. I think this is a reasonable thing for starship too.\r\n\r\nIt's also a bit less complicated than trying to query unknowable env vars that are outside the application edges.\r\nIf someone gets a zip with kitty pictures, cd into it, and then `starship allow`, thats on him if it contains malicious code imo",
    "author_association": "NONE",
